                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "startIndex": 1697,
              "endIndex": 2081,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "startIndex": 1697,
                    "endIndex": 2081,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Why this topic: Depop’s primary 2026 trend report identifies “Modern Uniforms”: dependable silhouettes, repeatable staples and less reinvention. This is a platform-specific international signal, not a measurement of Indian demand. Indian minimalist-wardrobe results also favour practical capsule lists, while recent community discussions show continued interest in repeating outfits.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "startIndex": 2081,
              "endIndex": 2437,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "startIndex": 2081,
                    "endIndex": 2437,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Distinctive angle: Start with clothes the reader already owns. Map a normal week across work, errands, dinner and rest, showing how a familiar shirt or pair of trousers can return in different combinations. Include a realistic laundry rotation and separate repeating a garment from wearing it unwashed. Avoid turning the article into a shopping checklist.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "startIndex": 2437,
              "endIndex": 2664,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "startIndex": 2437,
                    "endIndex": 2664,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Search targets: “how to repeat outfits”; “outfit repeating ideas”; “minimalist wardrobe India”. Proposed intent: informational and brand discovery. Priority: second. Confidence: high on brand fit, medium on search opportunity.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
                  "direction": "LEFT_TO_RIGHT"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "startIndex": 2664,
              "endIndex": 2957,
              "paragraph": {
                "elements": [
                  {
                    "startIndex": 2664,
                    "endIndex": 2957,
                    "textRun": {
                      "content": "Cottonworld fit: This directly expresses the brand’s slow-living principle—fewer unnecessary decisions and more use from everyday clothing. Mention a new piece only when it fills an identified wardrobe gap. Keep the existing broad slow-living article distinct from this practical weekly plan.\n",
                      "textStyle": {}
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "paragraphStyle": {
                  "namedStyleType": "NORMAL_TEXT",
